{
  "$comment": [
    "Anvil's machine-readable error codes. Operators branch on these strings, so they",
    "are a public contract: renaming or dropping one silently breaks an integration",
    "that was matching on it, and its `else` branch — usually 'proceed' — takes over.",
    "",
    "Regenerate with: node tools/regenerate-error-code-registry.mjs. The AST extractor",
    "is mirrored by error-code-registry.test.ts and",
    "counts a string literal only where it is USED as a code: a `code:` property, a",
    "`code =` assignment, the first argument to a *Error constructor, or an argument",
    "to a shared emit*/refuse*/reject* helper. A plain shape match would sweep in",
    "file paths like `reference/workflow.md` and MIME types like `application/json`.",
    "",
    "Enforced as a ratchet:",
    "  - a code emitted but not registered fails, so a new one is a reviewed diff line;",
    "  - a code registered but no longer emitted fails, so removing one is deliberate",
    "    rather than a silent break for whoever was matching on it;",
    "  - `asserted` may only go up. A code that had a test and lost it fails; a code",
    "    that gained one must have that banked here in the same change.",
    "",
    "`asserted` means some test in the workspace names the exact string. That is a",
    "weaker claim than 'the behaviour behind it is covered', and deliberately so: the",
    "contract being protected here is the string an operator matches on.",
    "",
    "Out of scope: certification check ids (`static/*`, `exec/*`), AIR predicate names",
    "(`anvil/*`), and MIME types. Those are contracts too, but different ones."
  ],
